Priya, Marcus, Tom,

Thanks for the time yesterday. A short recap so we're all working from the same list.

What we heard:
- Reno releases waves on a fixed 30-minute cadence, and the AMR fleet idles 20-25% of the shift waiting for pickers to catch up.
- Columbus and Allentown run the same Fulcrum build but different shift patterns, so Reno is the cleanest place to prove anything.
- Success for Acme means picks per labor hour, not robot utilisation.

Next steps:
- Priya will share two weeks of anonymised pick data from Reno by June 23 so we can baseline.
- I'll send a written pilot proposal with two scoping options by June 26.
- Tom and our solutions engineer Dana will compare notes on network requirements for the edge agent.

If I've missed anything, reply here and I'll fold it into the proposal.

Jack

